<title>NORWAY: UBN Q1 net profits fall.</title>
<headline>UBN Q1 net profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income		   613	 vs	   611</p>
<p> Net non-interest op. income	 481	 vs	   414</p>
<p> Operating costs			 709	 vs	   663</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p> losses and writedowns		 385	 vs	   362</p>
<p> Operating profit after losses     360	 vs	   401</p>
<p> After-tax result			264	 vs	   298</p>
<p> EPS Q1 (crowns)			7.17	 vs	   8.64</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's largest savings bank is Union Bank of Norway, known locally as Sparebanken NOR. The bank was seen to book first-quarter operating profits of 346 million crowns, according to a consensus forecast by six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
